    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 232356\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n456 PM PDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Chances for isolated showers and breezy conditions will stick\n  around through Saturday as troughing lingers across the region.\n\n* Dry and mild conditions resume next week with seasonable \n  temperatures.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through Thursday.\n\nAfternoon satellite imagery shows an upper-level trough churning \nover the Great Basin with a secondary shortwave pushing into the \nnorthwestern portions of our forecast area. As this shortwave \ncontinues to dig south, it will aid in the development of isolated \nshowers in areas of higher terrain north and west of the I-15 \ncorridor. This low will slowly exit the region on Saturday, \nresulting in low chances for isolated convection in eastern Mohave \nCounty tomorrow afternoon. In addition to isolated convection, \nbreezy northerly winds will pick up across the area tonight and will \nlinger into Saturday afternoon. Wind gusts will peak in the 25 to 35 \nmph range for much of the area, with the exception of Death Valley. \nWind gusts in Death Valley will peak in the 40 to 50 mph range with \nlocally stronger gusts possible in areas of higher terrain. A Wind \nAdvisory is in effect for Death Valley from 11 pm PDT this evening \nthrough 11 am PDT tomorrow. \n\nDry conditions and light winds will return to the entire region on \nSunday. Temperatures will gradually warm each day going into next \nweek, with near normal temperatures returning on Monday and Tuesday. \nA shortwave will move through the Pacific Northwest on Tuesday and \nWednesday, bringing breezy conditions to the southern Great Basin \nand knocking temperatures down a degree or two from Tuesday to \nWednesday.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 00Z Forecast \nPackage...East to northeast winds under 8KT will persist into the \nevening, backing northwest by 04Z.  A push of stronger northwest \nwinds are expected tonight, likely after 09Z. Gusts up to 25KT are \nexpected with these stronger winds with the push of winds, \nespecially at onset. Gusty northwest will continue through Saturday \nmorning into the afternoon, then will slowly diminishing 21Z. Gusts \nshould end by 00Z. Northwest will continue into Saturday evening but \nwill remain at 10-15KT for the first part of the night. VFR mostly \nclear skies will persist  through the TAF period.  \n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 00Z Forecast Package... Expect an increase in \nwinds overnight at most locations as a cold front pushes through the \nregion. Gusts 25-35KT are expected behind the front. Gusty north to \nnorthwest winds last into the first half of the day Saturday, then \nlikely begin diminishing late afternoon and evening. Mostly clear \nskies last through the TAF period. Other a few isolated showers in \nInyo County, it will be dry across the region.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Stessman\nAVIATION...Nickerson\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
